{
  "name": "RWC 2023 Semi-Final: England v South Africa",
  "description": "Stade de France, Saint-Denis - Saturday 21 October 2023. Rugby World Cup semi-final, 78,098 in the stands, Ben O'Keeffe refereeing.\n\nThe defending champions are in trouble. England, written off before the tournament, have turned the semi-final into a siege: Owen Farrell kicked four penalties to lead 12-6 at the break, Handre Pollard replacing Manie Libbok at fly-half after half an hour.\n\nNow it is the 53rd minute. Farrell has just dropped a goal from 40 metres and England lead 15-6. The Springboks, who survived France by a single point in the quarter-final, are nine points behind with the clock running and no try scored all night.\n\nYou are South Africa, about to kick off under Siya Kolisi. Nine points, twenty-seven minutes: make the bomb squad count, win the territory battle and find a way back into a World Cup final.",
  "win_text": "England 15 - 16 South Africa. RG Snyman's try, Pollard's conversion and a late penalty from halfway - exactly as it happened in Paris. On to the final.",
  "draw_text": "Level at the final whistle. In Paris, a late Pollard penalty edged it by a single point.",
  "loss_text": "England are through. In real life the Springboks fought back to win 16-15 - try again.",
